{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SECOND AND THIRD OCCURRENCE IN ONE HOUR — 2026-08-13, both on the macos-latest py3.13 shard only, every ubuntu shard green.\n\n- Gerrit **1715** (event_append split; confined to `src/rebar/_store/`) — GHA run 31680986340.\n- Gerrit **1716** (rich-text conflict-safety pins for story `disparaged-parodistic-shrew`; TESTS-ONLY, one new file under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`) — GHA run 31681638153.\n\nBoth failed on the SAME single assertion:\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`, at\n`assert any(\"declined 1 inbound link removal\" in m for m in messages)`. In both runs the captured records held the PER-LINK decline line (`_apply_inbound_update: declining the inbound removal of blocks link …`) but NOT the pass-summary line the assertion wants.\n\nWhy this is diagnostic rather than just another sighting: the two changes share no files, no lane and no author session, and 1716 cannot reach the assertion at all — it adds test code only. Two disjoint changes producing one identical macOS-only capture miss inside the same hour is positive evidence that the trigger is the shard's log-capture behaviour under xdist, not anything either change did.\n\nThe narrower signature also holds in both: it is the SUMMARY record that goes missing while the per-link record survives. If a fix is attempted, that asymmetry is the lead — the summary is emitted later in the pass, so the plausible mechanism is capture being torn down (or the handler swapped) between the two emissions on a worker, rather than records being dropped wholesale.\n\nBoth changes were rechecked on this basis."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786610709351124001,"uuid":"1332769a-38f6-4c3a-bee5-90f11d118980"}